<body>
    <h1>ECAS and Spring security</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>Spring security and ECAS can work together, in that case ECAS wi=
ll be used for authentication and Spring for Authorisation (The recommended=
 authorisation system in the Commission is ULYSSE <a href=3D"/CITnet/conflu=
ence/display/RefApp/RefApp+Ulysse+connector">RefApp Ulysse connector</a>.)<=
/p>
<p>For configure one application for use spring security with ECAS you can =
follow the steps:</p>
<ul>
<li>First install the <a href=3D"https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/CITnet/conflu=
ence/display/IAM/Downloads-WebLogic" rel=3D"nofollow">ECAS authentication p=
rovider</a>.</li>
<li>Add to the application the spring security dependencies:</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">=20
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: html/xml; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">&lt=
;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.springframework.security&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-security-core&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;${spring.version}&lt;/version&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</pre>=20
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>Add the refapp-support-security-ecas-file, this will add the authentica=
ted syntetic role</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">=20
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: html/xml; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">&lt=
;dependency&gt;
       &lt;groupId&gt;eu.europa.ec.digit&lt;/groupId&gt;
       &lt;artifactId&gt;refapp-support-security-ecas-file&lt;/artifactId&g=
t;
       &lt;version&gt;1.1.1&lt;/version&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</pre>=20
</div>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Add the spring security configuration in the web.xml (regular configura=
tion of spring-security)</li>
<li>Add the ECAS configuration in the web.xml</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">=20
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: html/xml; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">   =
 &lt;!-- ECAS security --&gt;
    &lt;!-- Here we specify which URLs are protected by ECAS and which appl=
ication server role is used.--&gt;=20
    &lt;security-constraint&gt;
        &lt;web-resource-collection&gt;
            &lt;web-resource-name&gt;refapp-uls-sampleappWeb&lt;/web-resour=
ce-name&gt;
            &lt;description&gt;Require users to authenticate&lt;/descriptio=
n&gt;
            &lt;url-pattern&gt;*.jsp&lt;/url-pattern&gt;
            &lt;url-pattern&gt;*.html&lt;/url-pattern&gt;
            &lt;url-pattern&gt;*.htm&lt;/url-pattern&gt;
            &lt;url-pattern&gt;/data/*&lt;/url-pattern&gt;
            &lt;url-pattern&gt;*.do&lt;/url-pattern&gt;
        &lt;/web-resource-collection&gt;
        &lt;auth-constraint&gt;
            &lt;description&gt;ensures that the principal is authenticated&=
lt;/description&gt;
            &lt;role-name&gt;authenticated&lt;/role-name&gt;
        &lt;/auth-constraint&gt;
        &lt;user-data-constraint&gt;
            &lt;description&gt;Encryption is not required for the applicati=
on in general.&lt;/description&gt;
            &lt;transport-guarantee&gt;NONE&lt;/transport-guarantee&gt;
        &lt;/user-data-constraint&gt;
    &lt;/security-constraint&gt;
    &lt;!-- Here we specify the ECAS login action URL (called after success=
ful ECAS login) and the ECAS error action URL.--&gt;=20
    &lt;login-config&gt;
        &lt;auth-method&gt;FORM&lt;/auth-method&gt;
        &lt;realm-name&gt;myrealm&lt;/realm-name&gt;
        &lt;form-login-config&gt;
            &lt;form-login-page&gt;/protected/login&lt;/form-login-page&gt;
            &lt;form-error-page&gt;/protected/ecasError&lt;/form-error-page=
&gt;
        &lt;/form-login-config&gt;
    &lt;/login-config&gt;
    &lt;security-role&gt;
        &lt;description&gt;Syntetic role that indicates if the principal is=
 authenticated&lt;/description&gt;
        &lt;role-name&gt;authenticated&lt;/role-name&gt;
    &lt;/security-role&gt;

</pre>=20
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li><p>In the weblogic.xml<br><br></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">=20
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: html/xml; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">   =
 &lt;!-- ECAS security --&gt;
    &lt;!-- Synthetic group/role to indicate if a user is authenticated --&=
gt;
    &lt;security-role-assignment&gt;
        &lt;role-name&gt;authenticated&lt;/role-name&gt;
        &lt;principal-name&gt;authenticated&lt;/principal-name&gt;
    &lt;/security-role-assignment&gt;
    &lt;!-- Only needed if you want to allow some resources to be accessed =
by authenticated=20
        users who do not possess any role --&gt;
    &lt;container-descriptor&gt;
        &lt;allow-all-roles&gt;true&lt;/allow-all-roles&gt;
    &lt;/container-descriptor&gt;

</pre>=20
</div>
</div></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Add the spring-security.xml with the configuration:</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">=20
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: html/xml; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">   =
  &lt;!-- J2EE pre-authentication --&gt;
    &lt;bean id=3D"jeePreAuthenticatedFilter"
        class=3D"org.springframework.security.web.authentication.preauth.j2=
ee.J2eePreAuthenticatedProcessingFilter"&gt;
        &lt;property name=3D"authenticationManager" ref=3D"authenticationMa=
nager" /&gt;
        &lt;property name=3D"continueFilterChainOnUnsuccessfulAuthenticatio=
n" value=3D"false" /&gt;       =20
    &lt;/bean&gt;

    &lt;security:authentication-manager alias=3D"authenticationManager"&gt;
        &lt;security:authentication-provider
            ref=3D"preauthAuthProvider" /&gt;
    &lt;/security:authentication-manager&gt;

    &lt;bean id=3D"preauthAuthProvider"
        class=3D"org.springframework.security.web.authentication.preauth.Pr=
eAuthenticatedAuthenticationProvider"&gt;
        &lt;property name=3D"preAuthenticatedUserDetailsService"&gt;
            &lt;bean id=3D"userDetailsServiceWrapper"
                class=3D"org.springframework.security.core.userdetails.User=
DetailsByNameServiceWrapper"&gt;
                &lt;property name=3D"userDetailsService" ref=3D"userDetails=
Service" /&gt;
            &lt;/bean&gt;
        &lt;/property&gt;
    &lt;/bean&gt;

    &lt;bean id=3D"userDetailsService"
        class=3D"eu.europa.ec.....MyUserDetailsBuilderServiceImpl"&gt;
    &lt;/bean&gt;</pre>=20
</div>
</div>
<p>And the class <strong>MyUserDetailsBuilderServiceImpl</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">=20
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import =
java.security.Principal;
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Set;
import javax.security.auth.Subject;
import org.springframework.security.core.GrantedAuthority;
import org.springframework.security.core.authority.GrantedAuthorityImpl;
import org.springframework.security.core.userdetails.User;
import org.springframework.security.core.userdetails.UserDetails;
import org.springframework.security.core.userdetails.UsernameNotFoundExcept=
ion;
public class MyUserDetailsBuilderServiceImpl implements UserDetailsBuilderS=
ervice {
    @Override
    public UserDetails loadUserByUsername(String username) {
        try {
            List&lt;GrantedAuthority&gt; userGroups =3D new LinkedList&lt;G=
rantedAuthority&gt;();
            String userId =3D null; // TODO retrieve the userId
            if (existsClass("weblogic.security.Security")) {
                Subject subject =3D (Subject) Class.forName("weblogic.secur=
ity.Security")
                        .getMethod("getCurrentSubject", null).invoke(null, =
null);
                Set&lt;Principal&gt; principals =3D subject.getPrincipals()=
;
                for (Principal principal : principals) {
                    if (Class.forName("weblogic.security.spi.WLSGroup").isI=
nstance(principal)) {
                        userGroups.add(new GrantedAuthorityImpl(principal.g=
etName()));
                    }
                }
                // TODO in the principals we can obtain all the data of the
                // user:
                /*
                 * Set&lt;WLSUser&gt; wlsUsers =3D subject.getPrincipals(WL=
SUser.class);
                 * if (!wlsUsers.isEmpty()) { WLSUser user =3D
                 * wlsUsers.iterator().next(); String uid =3D user.getName(=
);
                 */
            }
            if (userId =3D=3D null) {
                throw new UsernameNotFoundException("Cannot retrieve the us=
erDetails");
            }
            return new User(userId, null, true, true, true, true, userGroup=
s);
        } catch (Exception ex) {
            if (ex instanceof UsernameNotFoundException) {
                throw (UsernameNotFoundException) ex;
            } else
                throw new UsernameNotFoundException("Cannot retrieve the us=
erDetails", ex);
        }
    }
    public boolean existsClass(String claszzName) {
        boolean exists =3D true;
        try {
            Class.forName(claszzName, false, getClass().getClassLoader());
        } catch (ClassNotFoundException e) {
            exists =3D false;
        }
        return exists;
    }
}</pre>=20
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li><p>Finally is important in the configuration of the security:http confi=
g add the parameter:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">=20
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: html/xml; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">&lt=
;security:http auto-config=3D"true" use-expressions=3D"true"&gt;

    &lt;security:custom-filter after=3D"PRE_AUTH_FILTER" ref=3D"jeePreAuthe=
nticatedFilter"/&gt;
    &lt;security:session-management session-fixation-protection=3D"none"&gt=
; &lt;/security:session-management&gt;
    ..
&lt;/security:http&gt; </pre>=20
</div>
</div><p><br>With the PRE_AUTH_FILTER is set that the authentication is don=
e by a jee filter.</p></li>
<li>The session management fixation is important, if is not as "none" sprin=
g invalidates the current session and creates a new one, and all the mechan=
isms of ECAS doesn't work.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>A working example can be downloaded in the svn: <a href=3D"https://webga=
te.ec.europa.eu/CITnet/svn/REFAPPSDBX/security/ecas/refappSpringSecurityEca=
sSample" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">REFAPPSDBX/security/ecas/=
refappSpringSecurityEcasSample</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
